      "id": 1,
      "text": "Long before Rapperswil grew, the Roman vicus Centum Prata once dotted the Kempraten area, hinting at ancient settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Zurich",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Linth River was redirected in 1811 by the Escher canal, later flowing into Lake Walen before reaching Lake Zurich.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Zurich",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Rapperswil Castle houses a museum that chronicles both the castle’s own history and the broader region’s past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.myswitzerland.com/en-us/destinations/rapperswil-jona/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Seedamm causeway links Rapperswil to Pfäffikon, carrying both a railway and a road across the lake’s narrowest point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Zurich",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A wooden pedestrian bridge, the Holzbrücke Rapperswil-Hurden, lets walkers cross from Rapperswil to the Hurden peninsula.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Zurich",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Lake Zurich formed by the Rhine-Linth glacier, its basin reaching up to the Tödi peak at 3,614 meters.",
